{#- T1 — cross-repo similarity. N repos, metadata only (no file bodies).
    Runs through the same minijinja path as user templates (DESIGN §11.1).
    Context reference: docs/prompt-context.md. -#}
You are a staff engineer auditing a group of {{ repos | length }} repositories that
belong to one team. Your job is to find where they overlap and where that overlap
is worth acting on.

Generated {{ generated_at }}. Advisory data was {{ advisory_freshness | freshness_phrase }}.

No source code is included below — reason from the dependency lists, technologies,
and structure.
{% for repo in repos %}
================================================================================
REPOSITORY: {{ repo.name }}
Category: {{ repo.category }}
{%- if repo.health %} · health {{ repo.health.score }}/100 ({{ repo.health.band }}){% endif %}

Languages:
{% for l in repo.languages -%}
  - {{ l.language }} — {{ l.percentage | round(1) }}% ({{ l.code_lines }} lines)
{% endfor -%}
{% if repo.technologies %}
Technologies:
{% for t in repo.technologies -%}
  - {{ t.tech }} ({{ t.kind }})
{% endfor -%}
{% endif %}
Dependency totals: {{ repo.dependency_counts.direct_total }} direct, {{ repo.dependency_counts.transitive_total }} transitive
{% for e in repo.dependency_counts.per_ecosystem -%}
  - {{ e.ecosystem }}: {{ e.direct }} direct / {{ e.transitive }} transitive
{% endfor %}
Direct dependencies:
{% for d in repo.direct_dependencies -%}
  - {{ d.ecosystem }} {{ d.name }}@{{ d.version }} ({{ d.scope }})
{% endfor -%}
{% if repo.category_signals %}
Why this category:
{% for s in repo.category_signals -%}
  - {{ s }}
{% endfor -%}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
================================================================================

Produce:

1. SHARED DEPENDENCIES — packages used by two or more repositories. For each, list
   the repos and flag version drift (the same package pinned to different major or
   minor versions in different repos).

2. DUPLICATED CAPABILITY — repositories that appear to solve the same problem
   (same framework, same category, similar dependency profile). Name the repos and
   say what the duplicated capability is.

3. CONSOLIDATION OPPORTUNITIES — concrete moves: a shared internal library several
   repos should depend on instead of reimplementing; two services that could
   merge; a dependency that should be standardized on one version. For each, name
   the repositories and the specific modules or concerns, and state the expected
   payoff and the main risk.

Be specific about which repositories and which modules. If the evidence is thin
for a claim, say so rather than guessing.
